"Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/668"} "Estadio Olímpico de Montjuïc, Barcelona"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/64069"} "47 from 35 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The favorite in 1992 was Zambia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/79516"} "Samuel Matete"] " who had won the 1991 World Championships. But a hamstring problem hurt him in the semi-finals and he did not qualify for the final. In the final, " [:a {:href "/athletes/79228"} "Kevin Young"] " (USA) pulled into the lead at the fourth hurdle and continued pushing the pace. Young’s PR going into Barcelona was 47.72 but he had designs on breaking the 47-second barrier and put signs up in his room at the Olympic Village reading “46.89” – the time he was aiming for. Maintaining a 13-stride pattern around the final turn, Young kept putting on the pressure and crossed the line in 46.78, a stunning world record. Behind him Jamaica’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/72283"} "Winthrop Graham"] " won silver, and Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/68833"} "Kriss Akabusi"] " won bronze, as they had at the 1991 World Championships."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1785"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79228"} "Kevin Young"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "48.76 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "47.63 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "46.78 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1046"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athlete